---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const email = 'jamey@warrenlabs.com';
---

<Layout
  title="Support · Warren Labs"
  description="Help and support for Attune — the headphone voice-matching and preference-tuning Mac app. FAQ, troubleshooting, and how to reach a real person."
>
  <Nav variant="home" />
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Support</span>
      <h2>We're here to help.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Answers to the most common questions are below. If you don't find what you need,
        email us directly — a real person reads every message.
      </p>

      <p class="contact">
        <a href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Attune%20support`}>{email}</a><span class="muted"> — we usually reply within two business days.</span>
      </p>

      <h3>Frequently asked</h3>

      <details>
        <summary>What is Attune?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Attune voice-matches your headphones to the tonal signature of <strong>another</strong>
            headphone — as close as measurements can get you — then helps you tune from there to what
            <strong>you</strong> personally prefer. Everything is blind and loudness-matched, on your
            own music, so you're judging tone rather than volume.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What do I need to run it?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            <strong>macOS 11 (Big Sur) or later</strong>, on Apple Silicon or Intel — Attune is a
            universal app and runs natively on both. A pair of headphones and some of your own music
            is all you need.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I get started?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Pick <strong>your headphone</strong> and a <strong>target headphone</strong>, load a track
            from your Mac, then flip between <strong>Stock</strong> and <strong>Matched</strong>. Same
            track, same loudness — only the tuning changes. When you're ready, use
            <strong>Find your sound</strong> to fine-tune to your own taste.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I use my own music?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Point Attune at your music folder or pick a track. It only gets <strong>read-only</strong>
            access to the files you choose, and remembers your folder so you don't have to re-pick it
            every launch. Your music never leaves your Mac.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is Attune free?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>Yes — Attune is free to download and use from the Mac App Store. No account, no subscription.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What about my privacy?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Attune has <strong>no account and no network connection at all</strong>. It collects
            nothing, sends nothing, and works fully offline — your music, listening, and tunings stay
            on your Mac. Full details on our <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>The app won't open, or I can't hear a difference.</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            <strong>Won't open:</strong> make sure you installed Attune from the Mac App Store and
            you're on macOS 11 or later. Quit and relaunch; if it still won't start, email us with your
            macOS version and Mac model.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>No sound or "no difference":</strong> choose the correct <strong>output device</strong>
            inside Attune and check your system volume. The Stock ⇄ Matched switch is
            <strong>loudness-matched on purpose</strong> — listen for a change in tone, not a jump in level.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>My headphone isn't listed — can you add it?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Attune ships with a large library of measured headphones. If yours is missing, email us the
            exact <strong>make and model</strong> and we'll look at adding it in a future update.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do refunds work?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Anything bought through the App Store is handled by Apple. Visit
            <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a> to request a refund.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <h3>Reporting a bug</h3>
      <p>The more of this you can include, the faster we can help:</p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Your <strong>macOS version</strong> — Apple menu → About This Mac</li>
        <li>Your <strong>Mac model</strong> — e.g. MacBook Air (M2, 2022)</li>
        <li><strong>What you did</strong>, what you expected, and what actually happened</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it's something you can see</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Footer variant="home" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h3 { margin: 36px 0 10px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.65; }

  .contact { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .contact .muted { opacity: 0.55; font-size: 0.92rem; }

  .checklist { margin: 6px 0 14px; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .checklist li { margin: 0 0 4px; }

  details {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    padding: 13px 0;
  }
  details:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary::after { content: '+'; opacity: 0.55; }
  details[open] summary::after { content: '–'; }
  .answer { margin-top: 10px; opacity: 0.82; }
  .answer p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .answer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
